Given:

sin60° + tan30° + cos45° 

Concept used:

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/94e7340f2c47ba07e5da1d19152ecc63db883ae073c2e23fdca611ca147b7b52.png] 

Calculation:

sin60° + tan30° + cos45° 

⇒ {sqrt3} over 2 + 1 over {sqrt3} + 1 over {sqrt2}

⇒ {sqrt3} over 2 + sqrt 3 over {3} + sqrt 2 over {2}

⇒ {3sqrt3 + 2sqrt3 + 3sqrt2} over {6}

⇒ {5sqrt3 + 3sqrt2} over {6}

⇒ frac{3sqrt{2}+5sqrt{3}}{6}

**∴ The value of sin60° + tan30° + cos45° is frac{3sqrt{2}+5sqrt{3}}{6}.**
